60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Asuka**: Options are on the table. A is paid, B is lottery, C is shared racks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: Option C. My rain data shows the open racks are useless in winter. We need guaranteed, covered spots.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, covered spots are already taken. Option A. The ward park proves people will pay to avoid the hassle.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the neighbouring block’s fee drove two households out of meetings. I won’t risk that social fracture. Option B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Toshio, a lottery ignores the daily riders who need certainty. @Shunichi, a fee risks the exact isolation I fear. I need a middle ground.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Asuka, I hear you. But my sticker register shows daily riders would rather pay than be counted as one equal claim.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, that’s a preference, not a solution. My morning watch proved the physical bottleneck remains regardless of who holds the spot.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the bottleneck is a maintenance issue, not a pricing one. Option A funds the fix.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, funding the fix doesn’t fix the social rot. The ledger is empty, so A just shifts the burden. B is the only neutral ground.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Toshio, neutrality is just another word for indifference. I will vote for Option A, but only if we guarantee no one is excluded.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Asuka, I’m voting for Option A. The riders want certainty, and I’d rather pay than fight over spots.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: @Asuka, your guarantee is empty without enforcement. I vote B. At least the lottery is blind to who you are.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the lottery is blind, but the morning rush isn’t. I vote A. The ward park proves people pay for certainty.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the ward park is a business, we are neighbors. I vote B. It is the only option that doesn’t create debtors.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: Final vote. A: 3, B: 2. Option A is adopted.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,- **Yumi**: Yay! Option A it is. I’m glad we found a way that works for everyone.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: Fine. But if the morning rush doesn't clear, I'm taking my bike to the ward park.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the ward park has a fourteen-household waitlist. You’d be lucky to get a spot there.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, noted. I’ll draft the billing schedule. Just don’t expect me to do the reconciling.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
